<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARY C BANK TO QUOTE POLE, CZECH, SLOVAK CURRENCY.</title>
<headline>HUNGARY C BANK TO QUOTE POLE, CZECH, SLOVAK CURRENCY.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) will add the Polish zloty, the Czech crown and the Slovak crown to the currencies it officially quotes, effective on April 1, the NBH said on Friday.</p>
<p>NBH President Gyorgy Suranyi told a news conference Poland and the Czech Republic joined the Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development and fulfilled the International Monetary Fund's currency convertibility requirements, while Slovakia was close to reaching them.</p>
<p>The NBH also decided on quoting the three currencies as trade relations with these countries had developed substantially over the past few years, Suranyi said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
